course: dictionary
lesson: 8495
title: Sanitation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sanitation means the systems that keep a place clean and healthy: clean water, toilets, drains, and taking away sewage and rubbish. Context clues help you find this meaning. «Good sanitation stopped diseases like cholera spreading in old cities.» The words diseases and spreading tell you the word is about keeping people healthy.
explain: Sanitation is an uncountable noun, so we say good sanitation or poor sanitation, not a sanitation or three sanitations. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "Good clean water and drains stopped diseases spreading" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: Sometimes a word is used as a joke. «Sanitation engineer» sounds grand and important, but it is a joking or puffed-up name for a rubbish collector in the US. The words around it and a dictionary help you see when a word is not meant literally.
fact: Sanitation means the systems that keep places clean and healthy.
fact: Good sanitation includes clean water, toilets, drains, and taking away sewage and rubbish.
fact: Good sanitation helped stop diseases like cholera spreading in old cities.
fact: In geography, sanitation is a key need in developing countries.
fact: Sanitation is closely linked to hygiene, such as washing your hands.
fact: In the US, rubbish collectors are sometimes called «sanitation workers».
exercise: «Good sanitation stopped diseases like cholera spreading in old cities.» What does sanitation mean? | A type of old city building | A quick way to cook food | *The systems that keep places clean and healthy | A kind of illness
exercise: In the US, a «sanitation worker» does which job? | Builds bridges | Teaches music in school | Sells clean water in shops | *Collects rubbish
exercise: Sanitation is an uncountable noun. Which phrase is correct? | three sanitations | a sanitation | many sanitations | *poor sanitation
test: «Sanitation engineer» is a joking name for which job? | Famous scientist | *Rubbish collector | Water pipe inventor | Head teacher
test: Which of these is part of good sanitation? | *Clean water and drains | Tall buildings with no windows | Very big gardens | Loud music in the streets
exam: Why does good sanitation matter in a city? | It makes the city look bigger on a map | It stops people from ever feeling hungry | *It keeps places clean and helps stop diseases spreading | It only matters to people who collect rubbish
